  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "3Ogl3ULlxH0ehKJMPGI/yJkeDdk=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:01.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## Selection is the switch\n\nAn **editor** renders the inside of one document \u2014 one task, one contract, one budget row. A **drive app** renders the outside: the whole drive, a list of every task, a dashboard composing many documents into one view.\n\nThe rule that decides which one runs is not configuration, it is selection state. When a user has a drive open with **no document selected**, Connect runs the drive app. When they **open a specific document**, the registered editor for that document's type takes over \u2014 and the drive app can still wrap it as a shell rather than being replaced outright.\n\n## Picking the right one\n\nThe sharp line follows from the rule:\n\n| Goal | Right tool |\n| --- | --- |\n| Kanban board over every task document in a drive | drive app |\n| Rich form for filling out one contract | editor |\n| Custom file-tree sidebar for a drive | drive app |\n| Render and edit one specific task | editor |\n\nAnything cross-document \u2014 navigation, aggregation, a workflow screen spanning several documents \u2014 is drive-app work. Anything scoped to a single document's fields is editor work. Getting this backwards is the usual reason a \"dashboard editor\" ends up needing hooks it cannot legitimately call: an editor is handed one document, so reaching sideways into the whole drive from inside one is fighting the architecture.\n\n## Why it matters for shipping products\n\nConnect's default drive view is a generic folder tree, which is fine for storage and wrong for a product. Replacing that view is exactly what a drive app is for. The combination \u2014 drive app owning navigation and cross-document views, editors owning each detail view \u2014 covers the full surface area of a real frontend without leaving Connect and without building a separate SPA.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/02-Learn/05-connect/02-drive-apps.mdx (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:01.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:01.000Z"
    }
  },
